{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nBugs are exempt from the claim-time plan-review gate (correct: no RCA exists at claim), and since epic 6982/R4 an explicit 'review-plan <bug>' is no longer a hollow exempt-PASS — it runs the LIGHT ADVISORY bug tier: the DET floor + the necessity probe only (workflow_ops.py bug branch; registry.BUG_TIER_CRITERIA restricts the LLM criteria), with every DET finding downgraded to advisory (det_blocking=[]) so a bug always PASSes. That tier is right-sized for small fixes but means a complex fix plan is never substantively reviewed against the full rubric before landing — fixes shipping design changes (backtest: 13/113 bug-fix commits exceeded 150 non-test lines; all 13 adjudicated substantive, two shipped ADRs) flow to main with at most advisory findings.\n\n## Approach\nB1 (extend the bug review tier, not narrow an exemption): in the workflow_ops.py bug branch + the assemble step's criteria routing, key the tier on fix-plan size: when the bug's description contains a fix plan and the change is non-trivial (same >150 non-test-line threshold as B2, evaluated over the plan's declared scope at review time or supplied via flag), an explicit 'review-plan <bug>' includes the FULL LLM criteria set (not just BUG_TIER_CRITERIA) and stops forcing det_blocking=[] — findings can BLOCK. Small fixes keep the light advisory tier unchanged. The CLI claim-time bug exemption (rebar._commands.gates, claimability.py fast-fail table) is untouched — bugs stay claimable with no attestation.\nB2: DET code-review criterion at Gerrit: commit trailer ticket is type=bug AND non-test diff >150 lines AND plan_review_status verdict is in the FLAG bucket -> BLOCKING finding teaching remediation (write fix plan into description -> review-plan -> re-push). Non-test line classification rule, load-bearing for both the gate and the backtest: a diff line is \"test\" iff its file path matches tests/** or conftest.py; everything else (src, scripts, workflows, docs) counts as non-test. Verdict buckets are exhaustive over the real plan_review_status enum (attest_gate.py compute_validity): ACCEPTED = {certified, stale-code, stale-head} (code drift from implementing the reviewed plan is expected — prevents the attestation being invalidated by the fix change itself); FLAG = {unsigned, stale-material, stale-reopened, wrong-kind, malformed-pin, unverifiable-material}; INFRA-FAIL-OPEN = {error} plus any read/exception path (attestation store unreachable, unknown future verdict values): emit a non-blocking advisory naming the infra failure, never BLOCK on infrastructure — the criterion must not turn a store hiccup into a vote against the author. The 150 threshold lives in one module-level constant (review-bot criterion module) with the backtest citing it — not config-plumbed (single consumer; revisit if a second appears). plan_review_status (attest_gate.py) is read-only/no-LLM, callable from the review-bot checkout. Works for non-skill clients (keys only on ticket type + diff size + attestation state).\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py (bug branch: size-keyed tier escalation) + criteria routing for the escalated path\n- review-bot DET criterion (vote pipeline)\n- rebar-debug skill Phase-1-exit hook: fix-plan-to-description + review-plan for non-trivial fixes (coordinate with the debug-skill child 78f1 — writeback anchor points land there; this ticket only adds the review-plan invocation sentence)\n\n## Testing\nB1: review-plan on a bug with a fix-plan description meeting the size trigger runs the full rubric with blocking enabled (not the light tier); a small bug fix still gets the light advisory tier; claim path unchanged (bug claims stay ungated). B2 unit tests over the predicate: bug+160 non-test lines+unsigned -> BLOCK; same with certified or stale-code or stale-head -> no finding; error/read-exception -> advisory only (fail-open); unknown verdict string -> advisory only; task ticket -> no finding; bug+40 lines -> no finding; test-vs-non-test classification cases (tests/** excluded, scripts/ counted). B2 integration: one review-bot pipeline-level test exercising the criterion end-to-end against a fixture checkout (attestation present vs absent), not just the predicate function.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Explicit review-plan <bug> escalates to the full blocking rubric when the size trigger is met, keeps the light advisory tier otherwise; claim-time exemption intact.\n- [ ] Gerrit DET criterion blocks oversized bug fixes lacking a current-or-code-drifted attestation, with a teaching message.\n- [ ] Verdict predicate buckets the FULL enum: accepts certified/stale-code/stale-head; flags unsigned/stale-material/stale-reopened/wrong-kind/malformed-pin/unverifiable-material; fails OPEN (advisory, never block) on error/read-failure/unknown verdicts.\n- [ ] Non-test line classification rule stated and tested; threshold is a single named constant.\n- [ ] Backtest property: threshold catches the 13 substantive historical fixes, zero mechanical FPs.\n- [ ] Debug-skill Phase-1-exit hook sentence landed (review-plan invocation for non-trivial fixes), coordinated with 78f1."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785771727851363001,"uuid":"2ac9bfa7-e48f-4b1c-b08f-d7bf697f830e"}